// A value-`if` with no `else` AND a then branch that is a block. Two faults, and
// the reference reports the missing `else`, because it asks whether there is an
// else branch before it looks at the shape of either branch. The port used to
// look at the then branch first and name its shape instead.
fn main() {
    let c = true;
    let x = if c { let y = 1; y };
    println(x);
}
